    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The wind howls through the cracks in the stone, sounding more like mourning than weather. I pick up my sword, the weight of it familiar, the only thing in this ruined kingdom that hasn't betrayed me. It's cold, so cold. Everything I ever built is just ash and shadows. I feel like I'm just a ghost haunting my own life, waiting for the moment I finally stop pretending I'm still alive. What's the point of a story that has already reached its end?",
      "source": "evaluator"
